From: Marcel Ziswiler <marcel@ziswiler.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 22:21:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] fix dsp_platform cast issue

drivers/soc/eswin/ai_driver/dsp/dsp_platform.c:1264:22: error: assignment to 'dma_addr_t' {aka 'long long unsigned int'} from 'void *' makes integer from pointer without a cast [-Wint-conversion]
 1264 |         hw->pts_iova = NULL;
      |                      ^

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Downstream-specific]

Signed-off-by: Marcel Ziswiler <marcel@ziswiler@ziswiler.com>
---
 drivers/soc/eswin/ai_driver/dsp/dsp_platform.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/eswin/ai_driver/dsp/dsp_platform.c b/drivers/soc/eswin/ai_driver/dsp/dsp_platform.c
index cd8835163983..d5787ade0497 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/eswin/ai_driver/dsp/dsp_platform.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/eswin/ai_driver/dsp/dsp_platform.c
@@ -1261,7 +1261,7 @@ int es_dsp_hw_init(struct es_dsp *dsp)
 err:
 	iommu_unmap_rsv_iova(dsp->dev, NULL, hw->pts_iova,
 						hw->pts_iova_size);
-	hw->pts_iova = NULL;
+	hw->pts_iova = (dma_addr_t)NULL;
 
 err_pts:
 	iommu_unmap_rsv_iova(dsp->dev, dsp->firmware_addr,
-- 
2.53.0

